{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:10.1073/pnas.71.12.5004","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"4373738","source":"MED","pmid":"4373738","pmcid":"PMC434028","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC434028"]},"doi":"10.1073/pnas.71.12.5004","title":"A quantal analysis of the synaptic depression underlying habituation of the gill-withdrawal reflex in Aplysia.","authorString":"Castellucci VF, Kandel ER.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Castellucci VF","lastName":"Castellucci","firstName":"V F","initials":"VF"},{"fullName":"Kandel ER","lastName":"Kandel","firstName":"E R","initials":"ER"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"12","volume":"71","journalIssueId":330315,"dateOfPublication":"1974 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":1974,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A","title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","essn":"1091-6490","issn":"0027-8424","nlmid":"7505876","isoabbreviation":"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A"},"printPublicationDate":"1974-12-01"},"pubYear":"1974","pageInfo":"5004-5008","abstractText":"Habituation, one of the simplest behavioral paradigms for studying memory, has recently been examined on the cellular level in the gill-withdrawal reflex in the mollusc Aplysia and in the escape response in cray-fish. In both cases short-term habituation involved a decrease in excitatory synaptic transmission at the synapses between the sensory neurons and their central target cells. To analyze the mechanisms of the synaptic depression in Aplysia, we applied a quantal analysis to synaptic transmission between the sensory and motor neurons of the gill-withdrawal reflex. Our results indicate that short-term habituation results from a presynaptic mechanism: a decrease in the number of transmitter quanta released per impulse. The sensitivity of the postsynaptic receptor remains unaltered.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, U.S. Gov't, P.H.S.","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ganglia","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Synapses","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Gills","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Astacoidea"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mollusca"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Reflex"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Escape Reaction"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Synaptic Transmission"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Action Potentials"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Habituation, Psychophysiologic"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.71.12.5004"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC434028"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC434028?pdf=render"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.71.12.5004"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":170,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"